Fight engine 4.0.1, params 4.0.1-pre2024; 1229 fighters; N = 8000

=== API and determinism ===
PASS  API surface  (VERSION 4.0.1)
PASS  no learned model loaded by default: matchup = base tables
PASS  engine source has no Math.random
PASS  engine runs with Math.random disabled
PASS  same seed, same fight
PASS  same seed, same summary
PASS  trace on/off gives the same fight (400 seeds)
PASS  trace parity holds over a shared rng stream
PASS  worker-style concatenation (self.FightParams + self.MLRates + self.FightEngine) reproduces Node results
PASS  worker-style loadMLRates reproduces Node's learned-rate matchup

=== Engine v4: learned stat-line rates (loadMLRates / opts.ml) ===
PASS  matchup without a model equals matchupBase
PASS  with a model loaded matchup applies the learned rates  (distance attempt ratio Volk 0.87, Gaethje 0.94)
PASS  opts.ml === false keeps the base tables
PASS  params.mlWeight 0 keeps the base tables
PASS  opts.ml = { pred } reproduces the loaded model's tables  (max rel diff dRate 0.0e+0)
PASS  ML: same seed, same fight
PASS  ML: matchup is deterministic (same tables twice)
PASS  ML: trace on/off gives the same fight (150 seeds)
PASS  ML: predict(A, B) and predict(B, A) swap exactly
PASS  ML: swapping corners mirrors the learned tables  (max rel diff 2.2e-16)
PASS  ML: swapping corners swaps the probabilities  (Volk 69.3% as A vs 69.5% as B; base tables 62.1%)
PASS  ML: a fighter vs his clone wins about 50%  (50.1% of non-draws)
PASS  ML: Volk chin knob 1.6 raises Gaethje's KO/TKO share  (11.3% -> 17.0%)
PASS  ML: league-average pair keeps the league level (finish rate within 4 pts, sig landed within 8%)  (finish 53.5% -> 52.5%, sig landed 41.1 -> 39.6)

=== Engine v4: train-only priors (hidden-data protocol) ===
PASS  data/derived/priors_dev.json exists and stops before 2024-01-01
PASS  train-only priors hold fewer fights than the production priors  (Lightweight 406 vs 608)
PASS  params are labelled as fit on pre-2024 data (train-only priors and judging)  (4.0.1-pre2024)

=== Engine v4: judges (EM weights, shared + fight-level noise, 10-8 rule) ===
PASS  judge weights are the pre-2024 EM fit (data/derived/judge_em_train.json, cards before 2024-01-01)  (5519 cards to 2023-12-16)
PASS  an even round is a coin flip  (P(A) 50.2%)
PASS  judging is corner-symmetric (mirrored differentials mirror the round)  (86.8% vs 86.9%)
PASS  more output wins more rounds  (P(A) 86.8% for +6 head, +2 body, +1 leg, +1 TD, +30 s control)
PASS  10-8s come with lopsided rounds, rarely with even ones  (lopsided 63.9%, even 0.00%)
PASS  a lone knockdown edge usually wins the round  (P(KD scorer) 89.5%)
PASS  non-unanimous share of even-looking rounds near the data (MMA Decisions |EM| < 0.5: 43%)  (42.8%)
PASS  decision split and 10-8 share in a sane band  (UD 81.0%, SD 17.1%, 10-8 3.64% per judge-round)

=== Engine v4.0.1: point deductions and the cumulative learned-rate cap ===
PASS  deduction params set (judgecal: 2019-2023 decision rounds)  (ded 0.00515, ded2 0.075)
PASS  deductions leave the fight itself unchanged (same stats, same finishes; only the cards move)  (54 of 245 decisions changed at ded 0.2)
PASS  trace: per-round judges' scores add up to the cards after deductions  (537 points deducted in 245 decisions)
PASS  deduction points per decision match 2 x rounds x ded x (1 + ded2)  (2.10 vs 2.15)
PASS  at the fitted rate deductions stay rare  (0.050 points per decision)
PASS  learned takedown multipliers stay within mlMaxRatio (cumulative attempts and odds)  (TD attempts x4.00 / x0.250, TD odds x4.00 / x0.250 (cap 4))
PASS  mlTdLevel scales the learned takedown targets  (x1.20 -> x1.79)

=== Trace format ===
PASS  event kinds are from the spec table (+ esc)  (miss hit clinch break tdx td up hurt)
PASS  events carry t, k, w, s, snapshots; strikes carry tg and loc; subs carry name; fin carries how
PASS  event times are ordered within each round
PASS  all spec kinds occur over 300 traced fights  (miss hit tdx td up clinch break esc hurt pass kd recover fin reset sweep subx sub)
  sample event: {"t":38.73,"k":"hit","w":"B","s":0,"dA":0,"dB":0,"gA":0.8,"gB":0,"sA":0.976,"sB":0.95,"tg":2,"loc":"dist"}
  result: D DRAW | Majority Draw (47-47, 46-48, 47-47) | round 5 at 300.0 s | cards [[47,47],[46,48],[47,47]]

=== Symmetry and clones ===
PASS  swapping corners swaps the probabilities  (Volk 61.6% as A vs 60.7% as B; 4 se = 3.1)
PASS  swapping corners mirrors the 7 outcome bins  (max bin diff 0.9 pts)
PASS  alexander-volkanovski vs his clone wins about 50%  (49.1% of non-draws, 4 se = 2.2)
PASS  justin-gaethje vs his clone wins about 50%  (50.6% of non-draws, 4 se = 2.2)
PASS  league-average vs league-average wins about 50%  (50.6%)

=== Knob directions (Volk = A, Gaethje = B) ===
PASS  chin knob up on A -> more KO losses for A  (16.7 -> 24.3)
PASS  chin knob down on B -> fewer KO losses for B  (15.4 -> 10.6)
PASS  power knob up on A -> more KO wins for A  (15.4 -> 21.6)
PASS  output knob up on A -> more attempts by A  (212.2 -> 261.1)
PASS  accuracy knob up on A -> higher accuracy for A  (57.8 -> 66.3)
PASS  cardio knob up on A (tires faster) -> lower win share for A  (61.9 -> 54.6)
PASS  takedown-attempt knob up on A -> more TD attempts and control for A  (TD att 3.73 -> 10.01, ctrl 109 -> 216 s)
PASS  takedown-defense knob up on B -> lower TD success for A  (28.6 -> 16.9)
PASS  leg-kick share knob on B -> more leg kicks by B  (8.8% -> 36.4% of attempts)
PASS  submission knob up on A -> more submission wins for A  (3.9 -> 11.6)
PASS  judges.power up -> decisions shift toward the harder hitter  (Gaethje's share of decisions 27.4 -> 52.0 (damage/head 0.56 vs 0.85))

